lg.compare(lr0)
---
note: 3 of the 3,911 clusters hold one observation (line 2)
error[Z0416]: the likelihood-ratio test needs model-based standard errors, but `lg` has standard errors that are clustered by worker (3,911 clusters, CR1)
 --> scripts/main.zeff:5:12
  |
5 | lg.compare(lr0)
  |            ^^^ no likelihood-ratio test here
  |
  = help: `test` gives the Wald test of the extra terms under these errors: `m.test(a == 0, b == 0)`

